https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2lIy9SA3Y5g  (Capo 4) (MC3)

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord for the transposed (CaddG) adding the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  If you're not comfortable playing the (Bm) you may have trouble with this version.  I guess the good news is you can play another strum of (G) where the (Bm) is (in the verse but not in the bridge) and get away with it.

TIP:  In the opening and in the instrumental bridge I've indicated a (CaddG) between the (C) and (D).  You can play a (D4) if you'd rather but I find it more comfortable to simply add my pinky to the 1st string/3rd fret coming off the (C) before jumping to the (D), rather than try to hit the (D4) strait away and then lift off.  Whichever you find easier as they both work.  There's also a (Dsus2) at the end of a verse sandwiched in between two (D)s.  Just lift off your bottom finger.  Finally at the end of the chorus there's a |D7| in brackets.  Strum the (D7) once and hold, singing "a little bit" with no chord. 


